\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Per-model classification metrics on the scaffold-OOD test set. The 50\% binarisation absorbs much of the scale collapse that crippled the v1 regressors: even with negative R$^2$ on this split, accuracy and MCC remain meaningful. The no-information baseline (majority class on the test set) is shown as a dotted line.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:clf-per-model-scaffold}{{4}{9}{Per-model classification metrics on the scaffold-OOD test set. The 50\% binarisation absorbs much of the scale collapse that crippled the v1 regressors: even with negative R$^2$ on this split, accuracy and MCC remain meaningful. The no-information baseline (majority class on the test set) is shown as a dotted line.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
